<section class="card"><h2>Getting started</h2><p>Each operator signs in with their own account. Administrators prepare the house details and create accounts for the rest of the team.</p><ol class="guide-steps">
<li><strong>Review the house settings.</strong> Set the actual capacity, included guests, stay limits, contact details and policies. <?php if($user['role']==='admin'):?><a href="<?=ae(au('settings'))?>">Open House settings</a><?php else:?>Ask an administrator to make these changes.<?php endif;?></li>
<li><strong>Set the reference price.</strong> Use a monthly amount with a defined number of nights, or a fixed nightly price. The calculator shows the exact total, seasonal rates, discounts and fees. <a href="<?=ae(au('rates'))?>">Open Prices &amp; discounts</a></li>
<li><strong>Prepare the website.</strong> Save text and photo choices as drafts, preview them and publish when ready. <a href="<?=ae(au('content'))?>">Open Website content</a></li>
<li><strong>Add the team.</strong> Give operators the Staff role and keep administrator access for people managing accounts and settings. <?php if($user['role']==='admin'):?><a href="<?=ae(au('users'))?>">Open Staff accounts</a><?php else:?>Ask your administrator for additional accounts.<?php endif;?></li>
<li><strong>Configure email when ready.</strong> Until then, notifications are simulated. After configuring SMTP, approve delivery and queue a test to check the notification address. <a href="<?=ae(au('mail'))?>">Open Email</a></li>
</ol></section>
<div class="grid"><section class="card"><h2>Bookings and calendar</h2><p>Use <a href="<?=ae(au('bookings',['new'=>1]))?>">Create booking</a> for a stay received by phone or email. Enter an agreed total and a reason, or leave the total blank to calculate it.</p><p>An enquiry does not block dates. A confirmed booking or an active reservation does. The check-out date is the first free day, so another guest can check in that day.</p><p>Open a booking reference to change dates, guest contact, notes, payment record or status. Conflicts are checked again before dates are confirmed. Payment status is a manual record; this site does not collect money.</p></section>
<section class="card"><h2>Prices and publishing</h2><p>All amounts use THB. Enter <strong>1466.67</strong> for a decimal amount and <strong>10</strong> for a 10% discount.</p><p>A monthly reference of 44,000 THB over 30 nights is approximately 1,466.67 THB per night. A 30-night base stay is exactly 44,000 THB before any configured discounts or fees. A 31-night stay is prorated for the extra night.</p><p>Saving a content draft does not change the published website. Use the saved draft preview, then Publish changes. Uploaded images remain private until selected for the published landing page or published in the full gallery.</p></section></div>
<section class="card"><h2>Daily checks</h2><p>The overview shows enquiries, upcoming arrivals and failed emails. Background processing runs every minute and verified backups run nightly at 03:15 Bangkok time.</p><p>If an email fails, the booking remains saved. Correct the mail settings and retry the failed event. Simulated emails are never sent later.</p><p>Change your own password in <a href="<?=ae(au('account'))?>">My account</a>. An administrator can reset another person's password or deactivate an account. Older sessions are revoked after an account or password change.</p><p>The temporary public landing page stays available while the full site is being prepared. Public guest bookings require a separate launch review.</p></section>
